# partnership-opportunity-system

The partnership opportunity system implements core business logic for managing agricultural investment partnerships and territory allocations.

Key Components:

1. Profit Distribution Model (robson-business-plan.tsx)
- Three-way partnership structure with equal 33.33% distribution
- ROI calculations based on pig farming with market waste feed model
- Financial scenario modeling: conservative/standard/premium projections

2. Territory Management (opportunities/page.tsx)
- Geographic territory protection for partners
- Investment opportunity allocation based on region
- Partner qualification requirements and validation

3. Investment Structure
- Batch-based yield calculations (117.9kg per 5 pig batch)
- Zero-cost feed model financial projections
- Territory-specific ROI adjustments
- Investment ranges for different partnership types:
  - Goat cheese sausage franchise
  - Market waste collection networks
  - Regional processing facilities

4. Partnership Requirements
- Minimum facility specifications
- Market waste collection capacity thresholds
- Production volume commitments
- Territory exclusivity rules

The system focuses on sustainable farming partnerships leveraging the zero-cost feed business model, with territory protection and standardized profit sharing structures.

